@using OrchardCore.ContentFields.ViewModels
@using OrchardCore.ContentManagement.Metadata.Models
@using WorkMate.Records.Models
@model EditTextFieldViewModel

@*
    The alternate editor Orchard renders for a TextField whose Editor setting is "WorkMateLookup".

    WHY THERE IS NO DRIVER BEHIND THIS

    Orchard's own TextFieldDisplayDriver asks for the shape GetEditorShapeType(context) names, which
    for a field with Editor = "WorkMateLookup" is TextField_Edit__WorkMateLookup — this file. That
    is the same mechanism Orchard's PredefinedList text editor uses, and taking it means this module
    registers no field driver at all for TextField.

    That matters more than it sounds. OrchardCore.ContentFields already registers a display driver
    for TextField, and ContentFieldDisplayDriverResolver.GetEditorDrivers returns *every* driver
    whose editor predicate matches — so a second driver registered here for this editor name would
    render the field twice, and the only way to stop it would be to reach into another module's
    registration and narrow its predicate, in an order neither module controls.

    The driver's UpdateAsync binds m.Text, so the control below posting {Prefix}.Text is what makes
    a chosen value — or an unmatched one carried through untouched — arrive back on the field.
*@

@{
    var settings = Model.PartFieldDefinition.GetSettings<LookupFieldSettings>();
    var name = $"{ViewData.TemplateInfo.HtmlFieldPrefix}.Text";
    var label = Model.PartFieldDefinition.DisplayName();
    var hint = Model.PartFieldDefinition.Settings["ContentPartFieldSettings"]?["Description"]?.ToString();
}

<div class="mb-3" data-lookup-field="@Model.PartFieldDefinition.Name">
    <workmate-lookup name="@name"
                     value="@Model.Field.Text"
                     list-code="@settings.ListCode"
                     label="@label" />

    @if (!string.IsNullOrWhiteSpace(hint))
    {
        @* The field's own description, which the standard editor shows and which a reader would
           otherwise lose by the field being bound. Tenant-authored text, so it is written as text
           rather than as markup. *@
        <div class="form-text">@hint</div>
    }
</div>
